# Encrypted files are binary and must never be line-ending converted.
#
# A .levault is authenticated with AES-256-GCM: change one byte and it stops
# opening, permanently, and the plaintext it replaced was deliberately
# destroyed. Git's auto-detection does get this right on its own (every
# envelope has a NUL at byte 7, in the LEVFILE magic), but "correct by
# accident" is not a good enough guarantee for a file that cannot be
# regenerated. Say it explicitly.
#
# If you commit .levault files in YOUR repository, put this line in your own
# .gitattributes too.
*.levault binary

# The v1 vault fixture is a byte-frozen tripwire for the legacy Fernet path.
tests/fixtures/v1_vault/v1_vault.enc binary
tests/fixtures/v1_vault/v1_vault.salt binary
